---
title: Kuku Sabzi
description: Persian herb frittata
image: https://cookingwithayeh.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Kuku-Sabzi-7.jpg
source: https://www.notquitenigella.com/2024/04/10/kuku-sabzi-koo-koo/
servings: 4
---

= Egg Mixture =

In a large bowl, whisk the @eggs{6%} with the @fenugreek seeds{1%tsp}(ground), @salt{3/4%tsp}, @turmeric{1/2%tsp}, and @cinnamon{1/4%tsp}.

Add the @garlic{1%clove}(minced), @dried cranberries{50%g}(chopped), and @walnuts{75%g}(toasted and chopped) to the bowl and stir to combine.

= Greens =

In a food processor or by hand, finely chop the following herbs and greens: @parsley{70g}(leaves only), @cilantro{50%g}, @dill{20%g}, @spinach{100%g} (fresh or thawed), and @green onions{75%g}. Stir into the egg mixture.

= Bake =

Put a couple spoonfuls in a microwave-safe bowl, cover with a lid, and microwave for two minutes. Taste and adjust the seasoning as needed.

Preheat the airfryer to 160°C.

Pour @olive oil{1/4 cup} into the airfryer baking inset (about 20x20cm). Pour the herb and egg mixture over the olive oil and smooth the top.

Bake for ~{30%minutes}.

Carefully remove from the airfryer, flip the kuku over, and bake for another ~{12%minutes} until fully cooked. If needed, cut the kuku into squares before flipping to make it easier to handle.

= Serve =

Serve hot or chilled, alongside flatbread, cucumber, tomatoes, olives, jam, and feta.